In 2026, macroeconomic reality has flipped the question: <strong>"How can European sovereign economies attract and retain high-caliber young engineers, scientists, and doctors to prevent industrial contraction?"</strong>

The fundamental driver of European higher education policy is an unprecedented demographic divergence between aging European economies and India's youthful talent pool:

